<!-- partials.services.inbound-marketing-consultant.inbound-outbound -->
<section id="inbound-outbound" class="inbound-outbound">
    <div class="customContainer">
        <div class="header-holder">
            <article class="header-title">
                <h2>Inbound Marketing vs. Outbound Marketing - Understanding The Difference</h2>
                <p>
                    Before diving into the benefits of hiring an inbound marketing consultant, it's essential to
                    understand the key differences between inbound and outbound marketing. These contrasting approaches
                    to marketing each have their merits. It's crucial to recognize the one that best suits your business
                    goals and target audience.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="header-img">
                <img src="/assets/images/services/inbound-marketing-consultant/inbound-outbound.svg" alt="Inbound Outbound img">
            </article>
        </div>
        <div class="cards-holder">
            <article class="customCard">
                <div class="title">
                    <img src="/assets/images/services/inbound-marketing-consultant/inbound-icon.svg" alt="Inbound icon">
                    <h3>Inbound marketing:</h3>
                </div>
                <p>
                    Revolves around attracting potential customers by providing valuable content and experiences
                    tailored to their needs and preferences. The primary goal of inbound marketing is to establish trust
                    and build lasting relationships with your target audience. Inbound marketing strategies include:
                </p>
                <div class="list-holder">
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            Content marketing

                            <ol type="a">
                                <li>Blog posts</li>
                                <li>Whitepapers</li>
                                <li>Webinars</li>
                                <li>eBooks</li>
                                <li>Podcasts</li>
                            </ol>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Search engine optimization (SEO)</li>
                        <li>Social media engagement</li>
                        <li>Email marketing campaigns</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </article>
            <article class="customCard">
                <div class="title">
                    <img src="/assets/images/services/inbound-marketing-consultant/outbound-icon.svg" alt="Outbound icon">
                    <h3>Outbound marketing:</h3>
                </div>
                <p>
                    Focuses on pushing your message to a broad audience, regardless of their interest or needs. This
                    approach relies heavily on interruption-based techniques to capture attention, such as:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Television and radio advertising</li>
                    <li>Print advertising</li>
                    <li>Direct mail campaigns</li>
                    <li>Cold calling and telemarketing</li>
                    <li>Billboards and outdoor advertising</li>
                    <li>Email spams</li>
                </ul>
            </article>
        </div>
        <p class="short-text">
            Inbound marketing is all about attracting potential customers by offering value, whereas outbound marketing
            aims to interrupt and capture their attention.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

